428→<h2>Next Steps</h2>
429→<p>The intro sequence plays fully, but several features are needed to play the complete game.</p>
430→
431→<div class="next-steps">
432→  <div class="step">
433→    <div class="step-title">Input handling</div>
434→    <div class="step-status stub">Stub</div>
435→    <div class="step-desc">Currently returns neutral values. Needs to read the KN5000 control panel buttons via the SC1 serial port and map them to VM input variables (left, right, up, down, action).</div>
436→  </div>
437→  <div class="step">
438→    <div class="step-title">Sound &amp; music</div>
439→    <div class="step-status stub">Stub</div>
440→    <div class="step-desc">Opcodes 0x18 (playSound) and 0x1A (playMusic) consume their bytecode arguments but produce no output. The KN5000 sound hardware (sub CPU + DSP) is not yet understood well enough to drive it directly.</div>
441→  </div>
442→  <div class="step">
443→    <div class="step-title">Part switching</div>
444→    <div class="step-status partial">Partial</div>
445→    <div class="step-desc">Infrastructure exists (REQUESTED_NEXT_PART, initForPart), but bytecode/palette/video base addresses are hardcoded to intro resources. Needs bank-switching logic to load resources for all 9 game parts.</div>
446→  </div>
447→  <div class="step">
448→    <div class="step-title">Resource extraction</div>
449→    <div class="step-status todo">Todo</div>
450→    <div class="step-desc">Only intro resources (0x17-0x1A, 0x49, 0x53) are included. The remaining parts' bytecode, palettes, and video data need to be extracted from the original game files.</div>
451→  </div>
452→  <div class="step">
453→    <div class="step-title">Real hardware testing</div>
454→    <div class="step-status todo">Todo</div>
455→    <div class="step-desc">All development has been in MAME. The extension board target builds but hasn't been tested on a real KN5000. Timer prescaler behavior and INC instruction encoding may differ.</div>
456→  </div>
